// ============================================================
//  SHURI  -  personal pet robot
//  Wemos D1 mini (ESP8266) + 0.96" SSD1306 I2C OLED + TTP223 touch
// ============================================================
//
//  TOUCH
//    1 tap ........ NORMAL face, normal smile
//    2 taps ....... VERY HAPPY (^ ^ eyes, blush, big open smile)
//    3 taps ....... SAD   (droopy lids, tears, trembling frown)
//    4 taps ....... ANGRY (frowning lids, gritted teeth)
//    6 taps ....... SETUP MENU (same as holding 10 sec)
//                   every face lasts 5 sec, then back to the normal smile
//    hold 5 sec ... TIME & DATE, then after 5 sec automatically
//                   TEMPERATURE + HUMIDITY with your location at the bottom
//                   (tap = next page)
//    hold 10 sec .. SETUP MENU: shows the Wi-Fi she is connected to
//                   (tap = back, hold 3 sec = change Wi-Fi)
//
//  LOCATION (for the weather)
//    Without help Shuri only gets a rough guess from the internet
//    connection, and that is often a different city. Set the real place
//    from her phone page: type the town name (for example Karaikudi) and
//    pick it from the list. It is saved and used from then on.
//    The "Use my phone's location" button shows "Turn on your mobile
//    location" and asks the phone for GPS. Most phone browsers only share
//    GPS with https pages, so if it is refused, type the town instead.
//
//  BLUETOOTH
//    The Wemos D1 mini (ESP8266) has no Bluetooth radio, so the phone
//    link is Wi-Fi only. The setup menu says so on its BT line.
//
//  PHONE (Wi-Fi)
//    First boot : Shuri opens Wi-Fi "Shuri-Setup" (password 12345678).
//                 Join it on your phone - the setup page pops up by
//                 itself (or open http://192.168.4.1). Pick your Wi-Fi
//                 (home router or your phone's hotspot) and save.
//    After that : Shuri shows her address on screen at boot, e.g.
//                 http://192.168.1.23  (or try http://shuri.local).
//                 Open it on a phone on the same Wi-Fi to change her
//                 face and see time and weather.
//
//  WIRING
//    OLED  VCC->3V3  GND->G  SDA->D2  SCL->D1
//    Touch VCC->3V3  GND->G  SIG->D5   (TTP223, output HIGH on touch)
//
//  LIBRARIES (Library Manager)
//    Adafruit SSD1306, Adafruit GFX, ArduinoJson (v6 or v7)
//    (RoboEyes is NOT needed - Shuri draws her own eyes.)
//  BOARD
//    LOLIN(WEMOS) D1 R2 & mini   (ESP8266 core 3.x)
// ============================================================

